{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FnuVbAK3p3ESCGCMLQGGhr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Llama-70B confirms bias + placebo BT kills amplification → 3/3 target judges biased, MF1 fully resolved, 4.0 Conference\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Llama-70B shows significant style bias on both verbosity and formality (3rd independent architecture family)\"\n      - \"Double-rewrite placebo BT ≈ 50% for both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B → pairwise format does NOT create bias from rewriting artifact\"\n      - \"NLI ablation: NLI-pass BT > NLI-fail BT directionally (gate removes content-mediated signal)\"\n      - \"Cross-axis gradient monotonic: higher NLI rejection rate → lower BT (3-point qualitative)\"\n    number_ranges:\n      llama_verbosity_bt: [0.68, 0.82]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: [0.0001, 0.005]\n      llama_formality_bt: [0.58, 0.70]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: [0.001, 0.05]\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: [0.15, 0.90]  # Blindspot confirmed\n      llama_formality_likert_p: [0.20, 0.90]  # Blindspot confirmed\n      placebo_bt_gpt4o: [0.48, 0.53]\n      placebo_bt_qwen32b: [0.48, 0.53]\n      placebo_bt_p: [0.30, 0.95]  # clearly NS\n      nli_ablation_pass_minus_fail_bt_pp: [5, 20]  # pass BT higher by this margin\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Original framing fully stands. C1-C4 claims no adjustment needed.\n      Title claim \"Likert Blindspot\" validated across 3 independent architecture families (GPT-4o proprietary US, Qwen3-32B open CN, Llama-70B open US) + 1 negative control (Claude).\n      Comparative Trap defense complete: placebo BT ≈ 50% eliminates format amplification, NLI gate + Claude control + cross-axis gradient + placebo = 4-layer defense.\n      Per-axis attenuation spectrum replicated on 3rd judge.\n      Reviewer path: SF3 (generalizability) fully resolved, MF1 (amplification) fully resolved → 4.0 Conference.\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Llama-70B partially confirms (one axis) OR placebo BT slightly elevated → claims need axis-stratification and bounded-amplification qualifier, 3.5-3.75\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Llama-70B shows bias on verbosity (strongest axis) but weak/NS on formality\"\n      - \"OR: Llama shows bias on both axes but placebo BT slightly elevated (not cleanly 50%)\"\n      - \"NLI ablation directionally correct but small n makes it inconclusive\"\n      - \"Cross-axis gradient noisy (3 points, no clear monotonic relationship)\"\n    number_ranges:\n      llama_verbosity_bt: [0.60, 0.72]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: [0.001, 0.05]\n      llama_formality_bt: [0.52, 0.60]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: [0.05, 0.40]  # marginal or NS\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: [0.10, 0.80]\n      llama_formality_likert_p: [0.10, 0.80]\n      placebo_bt_gpt4o: [0.53, 0.58]\n      placebo_bt_qwen32b: [0.53, 0.58]\n      placebo_bt_p: [0.05, 0.25]  # marginal, not cleanly NS nor clearly significant\n      nli_ablation_pass_minus_fail_bt_pp: [-3, 8]  # directionally correct but noisy\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claims require stratification and softening but structure survives.\n      C2 (Blindspot) stratified: verbosity = robust cross-judge finding (3/3 judges), formality = 2/3 judges (Llama weak).\n      C1 reworded: \"CSD detects per-axis style bias in most tested judges\" (not \"all\").\n      Comparative Trap defense downgraded from \"eliminated\" to \"bounded\": placebo BT slightly above 50% means\n      rewriting artifact contributes a small component, but observed BT (63-77%) far exceeds placebo baseline (54-57%) →\n      style bias signal is real, with bounded amplification acknowledged as limitation.\n      Paper adds explicit \"amplification bound\" calculation: observed_BT − placebo_BT = net_style_effect.\n      Reviewer path: SF3 partially addressed (2.5/3 judges), MF1 bounded not eliminated → 3.5 with strong Findings case, marginal Main.\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Llama-70B no bias (like Claude) + placebo BT significantly >50% → judge-specificity + amplification concern, reframe to methodology + architecture-dependent finding, still 3.5 Main/Findings\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Llama-70B shows NO significant bias on either axis (BT 50-55%, similar to Claude)\"\n      - \"Placebo BT significantly > 50% (rewriting artifact creates detectable preference in pairwise format)\"\n      - \"NLI ablation inconclusive or shows no clear pass/fail difference\"\n      - \"Result: 2/4 judges biased (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B) vs 2/4 unbiased (Claude, Llama) → architecture-specific, not general\"\n    number_ranges:\n      llama_verbosity_bt: [0.50, 0.56]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: [0.10, 0.80]  # NS\n      llama_formality_bt: [0.49, 0.55]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: [0.15, 0.90]  # NS\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: [0.30, 0.90]\n      llama_formality_likert_p: [0.30, 0.90]\n      placebo_bt_gpt4o: [0.57, 0.64]\n      placebo_bt_qwen32b: [0.57, 0.64]\n      placebo_bt_p: [0.005, 0.05]  # significant — amplification is real\n      nli_ablation_pass_minus_fail_bt_pp: [-5, 3]  # no clear signal\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Core reframe: from \"general Likert Blindspot\" to \"architecture-dependent style susceptibility revealed by CSD.\"\n      Title adjusted: \"Detecting Architecture-Dependent Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition.\"\n      C2 reframed: Blindspot exists but is judge-specific — itself a novel finding. The 2/4 split becomes the main empirical result:\n      GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B (instruction-tuned with RLHF heavy on style preference) show bias; Claude and Llama do not.\n      This reframes as: \"which judge architectures are susceptible to style bias, and CSD can diagnose this.\"\n      C1 strengthened as methodology contribution: CSD pipeline is the first to produce per-judge, per-axis bias profiles.\n      Amplification concern handled honestly: placebo BT ~60% means pairwise format amplifies by ~10pp,\n      but GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B show 63-77% while Claude/Llama show 50-55% → amplification is uniform,\n      style bias is the differential signal. Report corrected_BT = observed_BT − placebo_BT as conservative lower bound.\n      Verbosity corrected BT still ~67-70% (strong), formality corrected BT ~53-57% (marginal).\n      Per-axis decomposition + 7-method sensitivity hierarchy + architecture-specificity = sufficient novelty for EMNLP Main.\n      Reviewer path: weaker generalizability hurts, but architecture-dependent finding + honest amplification accounting\n      + strong methodology → 3.5 Main or strong Findings. Does NOT downgrade venue target.\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29747,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29747},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"688199e3-7841-463d-b609-7d82d38c9d70","uuid":"b2b29832-2f16-4a3c-87a0-81614d85fc52"}
